    story: Pablo Drunkthorn was born in a monk farm family, where silence, breath,
      and repeated chores were treated as survival tools. As a child, Pablo Drunkthorn
      lived through a white road march, learning cold endurance and the cost of stopping
      too soon. As a young adult, Pablo Drunkthorn worked through a bone setter aide,
      learning where bodies fail and how panic moves through a fight. They enter
      the dojo to pay for medicine, debts, or mercy.
